course: dictionary
lesson: 13143
title: Forelimbs: front legs, wings and arms
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A forelimb is one of the front limbs of an animal. A limb is a leg, a wing or an arm. The word has two parts: fore means front, and limb is a leg, wing or arm. So a forelimb is a front limb.
explain: «The cat stretched out its forelimbs before it pounced.» The cat's front legs are its forelimbs. Ask yourself: what does this word point to? Here it points to the front legs of the cat.
explain: A forelimb does not always look like a leg. «A bat uses its forelimbs as wings to fly.» A bird's wing and your arm can be forelimbs too, because they sit in the same place on the body.
fact: A forelimb is a front leg, wing or arm.
fact: «Forelimb» comes from «fore» (front) and «limb» (leg, wing or arm).
fact: Humans, bats, whales and cats all have forelimbs with the same kinds of bones.
fact: Animals use their forelimbs for running, digging, swimming or flying.
fact: Scientists compare forelimbs to show that animals are related.
exercise: «The horse galloped across the field on its forelimbs.» What is a forelimb? | A tail | A back leg | *A front leg, wing or arm | A head
exercise: In the word forelimb, what does fore mean? | Under | Back | *Front | Inside
exercise: Which part of a human body is a forelimb? | Nose | *Arm | Foot | Ear
test: «A bat uses its forelimbs as wings to fly.» What are the bat's forelimbs used for here? | Swimming | *Flying | Digging | Running
test: Which of these is a forelimb? | *A bird's wing | A rabbit's ear | A cat's whisker | A fish's tail
exam: Why are the forelimbs of a human, a bat, a whale and a cat useful for showing they are related? | They all live in water | They are all the same size | *They have the same kinds of bones | They are all the same colour
